{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Transportation to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents relative to mobility matters.","BillNumber":"S2644","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J27","Name":"Joint Committee on Transportation","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T19:08:00.67"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2644/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, February 12, 2024 -- The committee on Transportation, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2206) of Joanne M. Comerford for legislation to prohibit video recording or broadcasting while driving; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2244) of Anne M. Gobi for legislation relative to electric foot scooter operating requirements; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2269) of Paul W. Mark and Vanna Howard for legislation to establish fast, frequent, and reliable passenger rail service between Pittsfield and Boston via Springfield, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2644).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Transportation be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 2206, 2244, and 2269 relative to mobility matters.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}